1
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:07,497
[Woman]
Jessica.

2
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:14,001
Jessica. Come on.
We gotta go.

3
00:00:16,249 --> 00:00:19,822
- Move it or lose it, sister.
- I don't feel good.

4
00:00:25,794 --> 00:00:29,538
[Kisses]
Mmm. You don't feel warm.
My stomach hurts.

5
00:00:29,611 --> 00:00:33,959
- Well, honey, if you don't have a fever-
- I don't wanna go to school.
I can do my work at home.

6
00:00:35,907 --> 00:00:38,109
Jessica, what's wrong?

7
00:00:40,227 --> 00:00:42,224
Everybody hates me.

8
00:00:43,911 --> 00:00:45,908
Oh, they don't hate you.

9
00:00:45,987 --> 00:00:49,194
They don't even know you
because they're too ignorant to try.

10
00:00:49,269 --> 00:00:52,339
I hate myself.
Jessica, don't say that.

11
00:00:53,656 --> 00:00:56,361
Oh, honey.
Look at me. Look at me.

12
00:00:56,436 --> 00:01:01,584
You are a wonderful,
beautiful little girl.

13
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:06,877
Don't let a few bad apples-
A few? Try my whole class.

14
00:01:08,223 --> 00:01:11,693
Remember the story
where the guy keeps saying
that he hates green eggs and ham?

15
00:01:11,773 --> 00:01:14,376
And then at the end
he realized he really loved them?

16
00:01:14,452 --> 00:01:17,728
One day, they're gonna realize
what a great kid you really are.

17
00:01:19,275 --> 00:01:23,623
You just gotta be like Sam-l-Am.
And don't give up.

18
00:01:25,437 --> 00:01:27,571
Okay.

19
00:01:29,891 --> 00:01:34,435
[Man]
That's it. Keep goin".

20
00:01:34,512 --> 00:01:39,329
Good. Nice.
You're doin'great, Jessica.
You're doin'great.

21
00:01:39,401 --> 00:01:42,380
[Kids Laughing]

22
00:01:42,449 --> 00:01:44,390
Hey. Hey, Seth.

23
00:01:44,459 --> 00:01:47,096
- You wanna spend the rest of class
sittin' on the bench?
- No.

24
00:01:47,171 --> 00:01:50,241
Keep goin', Jess.
You got 40 more seconds.

25
00:01:50,319 --> 00:01:54,703
My arm hurts.
Come on. Tough it up.
You can do it. You can do it.

26
00:01:54,772 --> 00:01:57,271
- My chest hurts.
- How do you think the ground feels?

27
00:01:57,351 --> 00:01:59,553
Hey, Seth. Two laps. Bye.
[Kids Laughing]

28
00:01:59,628 --> 00:02:03,201
Hey, Jess. It's just a stitch. Okay?
Just... keep breathin". You got it.

29
00:02:03,279 --> 00:02:05,276
[Panting]
I can't.

30
00:02:05,356 --> 00:02:07,729
Only 10 more seconds.
You got it.

31
00:02:07,799 --> 00:02:10,206
[Heart Beating]

32
00:02:17,076 --> 00:02:19,713
Jessica? Jessica?

33
00:02:19,789 --> 00:02:22,631
Jessica!

34
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:29,990
Oh, my God. Hey, go to the office.
Get Miss Parsons. Now!

35
00:02:30,070 --> 00:02:35,024
- [Cell Phone Beeps]
- I'm on the playground at Finley Elementary.
One of my students is havin' a heart attack.

36
00:02:35,093 --> 00:02:39,168
Yeah, she's 10. Don't you think I know that?
Just send the damn ambulance.

37
00:02:39,246 --> 00:02:42,062
Come on. Wake up.
Come on, sweetie.

38
00:03:19,629 --> 00:03:24,409
[Woman On P.A.]
Dr. Bender, call extension 2870.

39
00:03:24,493 --> 00:03:27,937
You ever seen
an infected pierced scrotum?

40
00:03:28,004 --> 00:03:32,952
Um, no, but I know a few people on whom
I'd like to see it happen. We need to talk.

41
00:03:33,022 --> 00:03:36,466
Well, if pain's what you're after,
the penis is really the way to go.

42
00:03:36,534 --> 00:03:39,202
- I'd recommend the apadravya.
- We're not talking.

43
00:03:39,277 --> 00:03:41,146
Oh. It sounded like we were.

44
00:03:41,216 --> 00:03:47,168
No, you're attempting to avoid talking
because you know what I wanna talk about.

45
00:03:47,236 --> 00:03:51,010
Nipples?
You need to get rid of
one of your people.

46
00:03:51,083 --> 00:03:54,321
Absolutely. As soon as
I do performance reviews.

47
00:03:54,394 --> 00:03:56,423
And then review the reviews,
of course.

48
00:03:56,501 --> 00:03:59,704
A decision like this can't be made
without proper, you know, review.

49
00:03:59,778 --> 00:04:01,943
Shouldn't take longer than a month,
maybe two.

50
00:04:02,021 --> 00:04:04,460
Four at the most,
unless it gets complicated.

51
00:04:04,528 --> 00:04:06,466
There's no way outta this.

52
00:04:06,535 --> 00:04:09,979
You might as well get it over with as fast
as you can, like ripping off a Band-Aid.

53
00:04:10,047 --> 00:04:12,715
Only instead of a two-cent piece of tape
and gauze, it's a human being.

54
00:04:12,790 --> 00:04:15,194
- Like you care.
- Like you don't.

55
00:04:19,111 --> 00:04:22,782
You have a week.
Get it done.

56
00:04:29,916 --> 00:04:32,914
We have a referral
from Dr. Lenkiewicz.

57
00:04:32,992 --> 00:04:35,431
- Don't know him.
- He knows you.

58
00:04:35,502 --> 00:04:37,839
- What's the problem?
- Heart attack.

59
00:04:37,909 --> 00:04:41,409
- Definitely don't know him.
- The patient's 10.

60
00:04:43,328 --> 00:04:46,668
Ten-year-olds do not have heart attacks.
It's gotta be a mistake.

61
00:04:46,739 --> 00:04:51,082
Right. Simplest explanation is
she's a 40-year-old lying about her age.

62
00:04:51,155 --> 00:04:55,032
Maybe an actress
trying to hang on.
I meant maybe the tests were wrong.

63
00:04:55,102 --> 00:04:57,941
That's what the E.R. Thought.
Three C.K. -M.B. 's were positive.

64
00:04:58,011 --> 00:05:01,477
The E.K.G. Shows classic signs
of S. T. Elevation. It's a heart attack.

65
00:05:01,557 --> 00:05:05,558
She's morbidly obese.
The "morbid" part of that raises alarms.

66
00:05:05,637 --> 00:05:08,133
Come on. It takes decades
to eat your way into a heart attack.

67
00:05:08,213 --> 00:05:13,161
Doesn't take decades to kill yourself.
If I was that fat, I'd be pretty tempted
to knock back a bottle of pills.

68
00:05:13,231 --> 00:05:18,944
It's not a drug overdose. The fatigue,
muscle pain and difficulty concentrating
have been bothering her for over a year.

69
00:05:19,016 --> 00:05:20,851
That's because of her weight,
her depression.

70
00:05:20,923 --> 00:05:23,956
That's what five pediatricians,
two nutritionists and a psychologist said.

71
00:05:24,033 --> 00:05:26,974
The heart attack would seem to indicate
that they missed something.

72
00:05:27,043 --> 00:05:30,144
- It's gotta be something genetic.
- What about metabolic syndrome "X"?

73
00:05:30,221 --> 00:05:32,751
[Chase]
Insulin resistance?

74
00:05:32,830 --> 00:05:35,532
Syndrome "X" could cause a stroke.
I don't know about a heart attack.

75
00:05:35,607 --> 00:05:39,278
- It could, if her blood pressure was high enough.
- Which is likely, considering her weight.

76
00:05:39,352 --> 00:05:44,961
Fits the symptoms. Me likee.
Do a hyperinsulinemic euglycemic clamp.

77
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:49,579
Oh, and one more thing.

78
00:05:49,654 --> 00:05:54,158
I've been told that I gotta get rid of
one of you guys by the end of the week.

79
00:05:56,243 --> 00:05:59,344
New sheriff. Belt tightening.
You know how it goes.

80
00:06:02,932 --> 00:06:05,428
Okay. Carry on.

81
00:06:10,158 --> 00:06:12,654
Some kind of game.
House's own version of Punk'd.

82
00:06:12,733 --> 00:06:14,671
It's not House. It's Vogler.

83
00:06:14,740 --> 00:06:17,681
We can't let it get to us.
We've gotta stick together.
Why?

84
00:06:17,750 --> 00:06:20,452
Are you suggesting
we start slashing each other's throats?

85
00:06:20,525 --> 00:06:24,995
I'm suggesting it's a zero-sum game.
Your loss is my win.
That's not conducive to team play.

86
00:06:25,075 --> 00:06:28,176
Which is what House seems to want.
Look, I'm with Cameron.

87
00:06:28,253 --> 00:06:32,894
It may be a bad strategy,
but I don't wanna give House
that satisfaction.

88
00:06:32,969 --> 00:06:36,413
- Come on. Sick kid, remember?
- [Door Opens]

89
00:06:37,518 --> 00:06:39,753
[Mother]
She's diabetic?

90
00:06:39,825 --> 00:06:41,922
[Cameron]
No, but it's similar.

91
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:45,500
M.S.X. Patients don't respond normally
to insulin, which causes
their body to create too much,

92
00:06:45,579 --> 00:06:48,851
and that leads
to metabolic abnormalities.

93
00:06:48,923 --> 00:06:51,830
We're going to do a test to be sure,
but there are certain dangers.

94
00:06:51,900 --> 00:06:55,103
Is this... thing treatable?

95
00:06:55,177 --> 00:06:57,446
It's controllable
through proper diet and exercise.

96
00:06:57,519 --> 00:07:02,798
Wait. Jessica already eats right,
and she exercises every day.

97
00:07:02,870 --> 00:07:05,309
I know you've already seen
several nutritionists-

98
00:07:05,379 --> 00:07:08,879
- And we've done everything
they've recommended.
- I understand, but-

99
00:07:08,958 --> 00:07:12,332
Why can't any of you doctors
see past her weight?

100
00:07:14,543 --> 00:07:19,582
If diet and exercise are the treatment,
then the diagnosis is wrong.

101
00:07:19,662 --> 00:07:25,203
It might be. But the only way we'll know
is if you let us do this test.

102
00:07:29,829 --> 00:07:34,299
It's really bad, especially at night.
It's like my heart is on fire.
Like it's, um-

103
00:07:34,378 --> 00:07:37,319
Oh, I don't know. Like, uh-
[Clicks Tongue, Sighs]

104
00:07:37,389 --> 00:07:39,383
Burning?
Exactly.

105
00:07:39,462 --> 00:07:43,270
Hmm, sounds almost like... heartburn.

106
00:07:43,342 --> 00:07:47,219
So, can you
give me somethin'?
Like a thesaurus?

107
00:07:47,289 --> 00:07:51,233
What?
I take it you never mentioned this
during any of your prenatal visits.

108
00:07:51,302 --> 00:07:53,240
Prenatal?

109
00:07:53,309 --> 00:07:55,782
[Sighs]
I'm not pregnant.

110
00:07:55,851 --> 00:08:00,161
Sorry, you don't get to make that call
unless you have a stethoscope. Union rules.

111
00:08:00,233 --> 00:08:03,072
I know when I'm pregnant, all right?
I have six kids.

112
00:08:03,142 --> 00:08:06,677
That's why my husband
had a vasectomy, and we use condoms.

113
00:08:06,755 --> 00:08:09,354
Vasectomies can reverse themselves.
Condoms break.

114
00:08:09,431 --> 00:08:14,106
Okay. This... is what a woman
is supposed to look like.

115
00:08:14,180 --> 00:08:17,155
Okay? We're not just
skin and bones.

116
00:08:17,224 --> 00:08:20,496
We have... flesh.
We have... curves.

117
00:08:20,569 --> 00:08:22,734
You have little people inside you.

118
00:08:24,716 --> 00:08:26,745
Okay, okay.

119
00:08:26,824 --> 00:08:30,701
I'm sorry. I guess I must have just been
brainwashed by the media...

120
00:08:30,770 --> 00:08:32,764
and all those years of medical training.

121
00:08:32,845 --> 00:08:37,018
- Damn right.
- I'll see if I can find some antacids
while the nurse gets some blood.

122
00:08:37,092 --> 00:08:40,227
Blood? Why?

123
00:08:40,304 --> 00:08:43,712
The heartburn.
Gotta make sure it's not... spreading.

124
00:08:49,334 --> 00:08:51,499
I don't want to.

125
00:08:51,575 --> 00:08:54,174
The test involves
some pretty precise measurements.

126
00:08:54,250 --> 00:08:57,852
If we don't know exactly how much you weigh,
we won't get the right answers.

127
00:09:00,237 --> 00:09:04,980
Let me tell you a secret.
When I was your age, I was heavy too.

128
00:09:05,054 --> 00:09:06,786
Were you over a hundred?

129
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:11,330
[Chuckles]
Way over. Kids in my neighborhood
used to call me "Rerun."

130
00:09:11,410 --> 00:09:16,381
Rerun?
He was a heavy guy from TV.
L- I used to pretend I liked it, but I didn't.

131
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:18,523
How come
you're not heavy anymore?

132
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:21,633
Ninth grade, grew five inches.
Everything kind of evened out.

133
00:09:23,049 --> 00:09:25,043
You think that'll happen to me?
Well, yeah.

134
00:09:25,123 --> 00:09:30,368
Your mom's tall,
and you are a little short for your age.
Probably spring right up.

135
00:09:40,475 --> 00:09:43,473
[Chase]
Obesity isn't something
you just grow out of.

136
00:09:43,552 --> 00:09:47,189
I take it you've never seen a baby?
She's not a baby. She's 10.

137
00:09:47,265 --> 00:09:50,537
And you figure making her feel like crap
would do her a world of good?

138
00:09:50,609 --> 00:09:54,748
- Yeah, if it gets her off the couch.
- I'm sure she's already
under enough pressure.

139
00:09:54,824 --> 00:09:58,426
Not from Mummy.
Everything in society tells us
we have to be thin to be successful.

140
00:09:58,503 --> 00:10:02,277
No. Society tells you you have to be thin
to be attractive. And guess what?

141
00:10:02,350 --> 00:10:05,451
That's what attractive means,
that society likes looking at you.

142
00:10:05,527 --> 00:10:09,266
I think we should be telling our kids
it's fine as long as they're healthy.
Right.

143
00:10:09,340 --> 00:10:12,806
You weigh 90 pounds
because it makes you healthier?

144
00:10:12,886 --> 00:10:17,697
Forget it. He's just cranky because he knows
he's the one who's gonna get the ax.

145
00:10:23,288 --> 00:10:25,282
So, any thoughts?

146
00:10:25,361 --> 00:10:28,268
On what? Sharon's plan for Gaza?

147
00:10:28,338 --> 00:10:31,074
Who you gonna let go?

148
00:10:31,148 --> 00:10:36,187
I'm thinking I can convince Vogler it would
be more cost-efficient to keep all of them.
Yeah, you should be able to pull that off.

149
00:10:36,266 --> 00:10:38,796
Most billionaires
aren't very good with numbers.

150
00:10:38,874 --> 00:10:44,553
It will be more cost-efficient
once I grab Cameron's ass,
call Foreman a spade, and Chase-

151
00:10:44,626 --> 00:10:48,070
Well, I'll grab his ass too.

152
00:10:48,139 --> 00:10:53,110
You are uniquely talented in many areas,
but office politics is not one of them.

153
00:10:53,190 --> 00:10:55,425
Don't take Vogler on.

154
00:10:55,498 --> 00:10:57,994
- Separate or together?
- Together.

155
00:10:58,073 --> 00:11:01,048
[Cash Register Beeps]

156
00:11:02,087 --> 00:11:05,461
Increasing glucose
to 6.9 milligrams per minute.

157
00:11:05,532 --> 00:11:07,835
- [Cameron]
Are you okay?
- I'm thirsty.

158
00:11:07,907 --> 00:11:10,541
- Just a little bit longer,
and you'll be done.
- Like Dr. Chase.

159
00:11:10,615 --> 00:11:12,712
Wanna put some money on it?

160
00:11:15,934 --> 00:11:18,338
I said I'm thirsty.
Just five more minutes.

161
00:11:18,409 --> 00:11:21,111
Okay, sweetheart?
I'm not your sweetheart.
Don't call me that.

162
00:11:21,184 --> 00:11:23,783
- Jessica, that's not nice.
- They're the ones who aren't nice.

163
00:11:23,862 --> 00:11:26,701
Jessica.
You're not, either.
I don't wanna do this anymore.

164
00:11:26,770 --> 00:11:29,107
Jessica. Jessica,
you have to calm down.
No.! No.!

165
00:11:29,179 --> 00:11:31,150
[Groans]
Let me go.

166
00:11:31,219 --> 00:11:33,213
Check her blood sugar.
She's gotta be getting hypoglycemic.

167
00:11:33,293 --> 00:11:36,326
I've never seen her like this before.
Something's wrong.

168
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:39,243
Let go of me!
Get it out of me!

169
00:11:39,313 --> 00:11:42,813
Let go of me, you son of a bitch!
You bastard!

170
00:11:42,892 --> 00:11:46,928
- Oh, no.
- [Screaming]

171
00:11:48,779 --> 00:11:51,686
She's sedated.
Mrs. Simms, don't worry.

172
00:11:51,756 --> 00:11:56,727
Hypoglycemia can cause temporary psychosis
and is a common complication
during an H.E.C. Procedure.

173
00:11:56,807 --> 00:11:58,870
I never wanted it done
in the first place.

174
00:11:58,947 --> 00:12:02,048
We understand you're upset-
You were supposed
to be monitoring her condition,

175
00:12:02,124 --> 00:12:04,187
but instead you were bickering
and placing bets.

176
00:12:04,266 --> 00:12:08,439
I apologize if it looked like
we weren't devoting our full attention
to your daughter, but I assure you-

177
00:12:08,513 --> 00:12:12,755
Oh, please. Save your pathetic insincerity
for your boyfriend.

178
00:12:12,828 --> 00:12:17,275
You're wrong.
She is, in fact, pathetically sincere.
And they didn't screw it up.

179
00:12:17,343 --> 00:12:20,284
- Who are you?
- I'm from the lab.

180
00:12:20,354 --> 00:12:26,033
The blood tests show your daughter was not
hypoglycemic, which means her psychosis
wasn't caused by anything these doctors did.

181
00:12:26,106 --> 00:12:30,073
- So then what was it caused by?
- I've no idea.

182
00:12:30,153 --> 00:12:33,824
Huh.
But you'll be happy to hear
it cannot be cured by diet or exercise.

183
00:12:45,507 --> 00:12:50,182
What else could cause
uncontrollable rage in a 10-year-old?

184
00:12:50,256 --> 00:12:52,227
Nothing that could
also cause a heart attack.

185
00:12:54,671 --> 00:13:00,053
I assume I don't have to point out
that now would be an extremely good time...

186
00:13:00,123 --> 00:13:04,193
for one of you to distinguish yourself
with a brilliant idea.

187
00:13:09,154 --> 00:13:11,217
A hypercoagulable state
can cause a blood clot.

188
00:13:11,293 --> 00:13:15,705
- Blood clots can cause a heart attack.
- More likely to cause a stroke,
not the psychosis.

189
00:13:15,776 --> 00:13:20,486
No, you're wrong. If a clot made it
to the amygdala area of the brain,
it might cause uncontrollable rage.

190
00:13:20,559 --> 00:13:24,196
Right, because anything's possible,
but nothing's gonna cause multiple clots
in a kid this age.

191
00:13:24,272 --> 00:13:27,510
- She's fat.
- Obesity doesn't cause blood clots.

192
00:13:27,583 --> 00:13:29,646
[Chase]
Extremely obese patients
can get a fat embolus.

193
00:13:29,723 --> 00:13:32,596
Right, after they've had liposuction,
which she's clearly never had.

194
00:13:32,667 --> 00:13:35,470
- How do you know?
- Because we have her medical records,

195
00:13:35,544 --> 00:13:39,488
and because no plastic surgeon in his right
mind is gonna give a 10-year-old liposuction.

196
00:13:39,557 --> 00:13:42,430
Have you ever met a plastic surgeon
who was in their right mind?

197
00:13:43,938 --> 00:13:46,936
- She hasn't had liposuction.
- Thank you.

198
00:13:47,986 --> 00:13:50,893
But what about some other
ridiculous obesity treatment?

199
00:13:50,962 --> 00:13:54,701
Like what?
Diet pills can cause heart attacks
and blood clots.

200
00:13:54,776 --> 00:13:59,246
- Her tox screen was negative.
- Wouldn't show over-the-counter
weight loss drugs.

201
00:13:59,325 --> 00:14:02,893
Her mother wouldn't give her diet pills.
She thinks her daughter's perfect
just the way she is.

202
00:14:02,971 --> 00:14:05,274
She's lying.

203
00:14:06,550 --> 00:14:09,890
Okay. You two, heparin
and warfarin to prevent further clotting.

204
00:14:10,864 --> 00:14:13,394
And you find those pills.

205
00:14:14,944 --> 00:14:18,388
- [Door Opens]
- [Pills Rattling]

206
00:14:19,962 --> 00:14:21,900
[Door Opens]

207
00:14:23,407 --> 00:14:26,176
Not diet pills.

208
00:14:27,822 --> 00:14:29,816
You might wanna broaden
the search just a little.

209
00:14:29,895 --> 00:14:32,265
And don'tjust ask the mom.

210
00:14:32,337 --> 00:14:36,338
If she hasn't mentioned it yet, she's not-
If you're gonna fire someone,
go ahead and do it.

211
00:14:36,418 --> 00:14:41,527
But don't treat us like lab rats,
testing how long it takes
to get us at one another's throats.

212
00:14:41,601 --> 00:14:43,904
- So what should I do?
- I don't give a damn what you do.

213
00:14:43,976 --> 00:14:48,218
Yes, I had noticed
your complete indifference.

214
00:14:48,292 --> 00:14:51,165
You don't even offer
a medical opinion anymore.

215
00:14:51,235 --> 00:14:55,179
- Who would you fire?
- Not my call.

216
00:14:55,249 --> 00:14:57,484
I want your opinion.

217
00:14:57,556 --> 00:15:00,325
Fine, it's you.

218
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:02,999
Either way,
you're making a choice.

219
00:15:05,718 --> 00:15:07,656
Chase.

220
00:15:09,430 --> 00:15:12,702
- Because he screwed up an angio
a month ago?
- Anyone can make a mistake.

221
00:15:12,775 --> 00:15:16,982
Right. So it's the money.
You resent it, but you're gonna tell me
that he doesn't need the job.

222
00:15:17,056 --> 00:15:19,153
He doesn't appreciate the job.

223
00:15:19,231 --> 00:15:22,264
He was ready to go three rounds
with Cameron for it.

224
00:15:22,341 --> 00:15:25,180
He wants the job.
He just doesn't appreciate it.

225
00:15:25,251 --> 00:15:30,062
There's nothing wrong
with just wanting to hang out,
but this is not the place to do it.

226
00:15:31,707 --> 00:15:34,979
- I'm surprised.
- You thought I'd pick Cameron?

227
00:15:35,050 --> 00:15:37,147
I didn't think you'd pick at all.

228
00:15:41,105 --> 00:15:43,408
[Elevator Bell Dings]

229
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:46,888
Guess he's not the "rise above the fray" guy
he'd like us to think he is.

230
00:15:46,958 --> 00:15:48,952
You practically forced it out of him.

231
00:15:49,033 --> 00:15:51,906
He's scared of losing his job,
just like everybody else.

232
00:15:51,975 --> 00:15:54,950
I've been thinking. You've made it quite
clear that you're miserable here.

233
00:15:55,019 --> 00:15:58,291
I am not miserable.
You're not happy.

234
00:15:58,364 --> 00:16:01,738
And you are?
With my job, yes.

235
00:16:01,809 --> 00:16:05,047
I am exactly where I wanna be,
doing exactly what I wanna do.

236
00:16:05,121 --> 00:16:08,393
Think I sense a hint of sarcasm there.

237
00:16:08,465 --> 00:16:13,574
Why don't you pick yourself? Quit?
Hmm, I was wrong.

238
00:16:13,649 --> 00:16:18,119
About Vogler or Foreman?
Mrs. Hernandez's pregnancy test.

239
00:16:18,198 --> 00:16:23,273
Who's Mrs. Hernandez?
Either a woman carrying an alien baby
or your newest patient.

240
00:16:24,787 --> 00:16:28,322
So you never saw her with any pills.
She never mentioned anything?

241
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:30,703
No, of course not.

242
00:16:30,775 --> 00:16:33,578
Would it be all right if I, uh,
talk to a couple of her friends?

243
00:16:33,651 --> 00:16:35,622
Her friends?
I'm not gonna interrogate them.

244
00:16:35,691 --> 00:16:38,963
I just wanna ask ifJessica
ever mentioned anything.

245
00:16:39,037 --> 00:16:41,100
It's- It's pretty important.
She's very sick.

246
00:16:41,176 --> 00:16:43,912
I understand. It's just, well-

247
00:16:43,986 --> 00:16:46,185
Jessica really
doesn't have any friends.

248
00:16:46,261 --> 00:16:48,496
Not one?
I've tried to help,

249
00:16:48,568 --> 00:16:51,041
make the kids include her more,
but... kids can be-

250
00:16:51,111 --> 00:16:53,481
- Kids?
- I was gonna say jerks.

251
00:16:53,553 --> 00:16:55,524
[Bell Rings]

252
00:16:55,593 --> 00:16:57,963
All the fifth-graders are assigned
an eighth-grade buddy.

253
00:16:58,034 --> 00:16:59,972
Maybe you could talk to hers.

254
00:17:05,694 --> 00:17:08,133
What's the status on House?

255
00:17:08,201 --> 00:17:12,044
He asked for time to complete performance
reviews for everyone in his department.

256
00:17:12,116 --> 00:17:14,110
And you told him no
and gave him how long?

257
00:17:14,189 --> 00:17:17,222
A week. He'll do it.

258
00:17:17,299 --> 00:17:21,837
Guy's never done what he's told.
I don't see why he's gonna start now.

259
00:17:22,986 --> 00:17:25,185
Hi. Edward Vogler.

260
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:28,327
Is Dr. House claiming that
I'm forcing him to get rid of one of you?

261
00:17:28,405 --> 00:17:31,107
I assume his goal is to stir up
antagonism toward me.

262
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:35,855
- And your goal is?
- I am forcing him.

263
00:17:35,930 --> 00:17:39,202
I'll do whatever I can to ease
the transition for whoever he chooses.

264
00:17:39,274 --> 00:17:43,218
- If you're feeling guilty about your decision,
there is an easy solution.
- I don't feel guilty.

265
00:17:43,288 --> 00:17:46,890
Then... why approach me
and tell me all this?

266
00:17:46,968 --> 00:17:49,636
I don't feel guilty.
That doesn't mean I don't feel bad.

267
00:17:49,710 --> 00:17:52,114
I'm rich, but I'm still human.

268
00:17:53,423 --> 00:17:55,361
I just wanted you to know...

269
00:17:55,430 --> 00:17:59,535
that if there's anything
I can do for you, my door's open.

270
00:17:59,611 --> 00:18:01,742
Thank you.

271
00:18:08,307 --> 00:18:12,583
You're lookin' for info?
Thought you already
had House all figured out.

272
00:18:12,655 --> 00:18:15,790
I do. Don't know his team though.

273
00:18:18,141 --> 00:18:21,447
[Wilson]
The ultrasound and biopsy
confirmed our worry.

274
00:18:21,519 --> 00:18:25,829
The tumor is extremely large,
at least 30 pounds.

275
00:18:25,901 --> 00:18:29,002
Oh, God.
It's actually a personal record
for this clinic.

276
00:18:29,078 --> 00:18:32,715
But it's completely benign.
There's no sign of cancer at all.

277
00:18:32,791 --> 00:18:34,820
[Gasps, Sniffles]

278
00:18:34,898 --> 00:18:37,999
I've already spoken
with Dr. Bergin, and he's available
first thing in the morning.

279
00:18:38,076 --> 00:18:40,014
For what?

280
00:18:42,023 --> 00:18:43,961
For the surgery.

281
00:18:44,030 --> 00:18:47,302
But if it's not cancer,
it can't kill me, right?

282
00:18:50,551 --> 00:18:52,888
Mmm, no.
I'll have a huge scar.

283
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:55,799
I won't be able to wear a bikini.

284
00:18:55,870 --> 00:18:59,314
- You wear a bikini now?
- Yeah. You got a problem with that?

285
00:18:59,382 --> 00:19:02,323
Nope. But I've never
gone swimming with you.

286
00:19:02,392 --> 00:19:05,128
I knew it.
That's what this is all about.

287
00:19:05,202 --> 00:19:08,976
You are trying to force me
to have cosmetic surgery.

288
00:19:09,048 --> 00:19:13,049
Yeah, that's exactly why I planted
a 30-pound tumor on your ovary.

289
00:19:13,129 --> 00:19:17,633
It's not gonna kill me. The only thing
surgery is gonna do is change the way I look.

290
00:19:17,711 --> 00:19:21,747
That is the definition
of cosmetic surgery.

291
00:19:21,824 --> 00:19:24,993
Uh, it would also relieve
your heartburn and discomfort.

292
00:19:25,069 --> 00:19:28,740
Yeah, right. Why give an antacid
if you can cut someone up...

293
00:19:28,816 --> 00:19:30,879
and make them
a little easier on your eyes?

294
00:19:32,962 --> 00:19:38,207
My husband... loves my body.
He can't get enough of it.

295
00:19:38,282 --> 00:19:42,625
You think he's gonna wanna touch me
if I look like I've been gutted like a fish?

296
00:19:44,468 --> 00:19:47,443
[Door Closes]
That was unexpected.

297
00:19:49,419 --> 00:19:51,413
Yeah, it was.

298
00:19:52,865 --> 00:19:55,430
All she does during recess
is run laps around the playground.

299
00:19:55,506 --> 00:19:59,542
She says she's exercising,
but everyone knows it's just because
no one wants to play with her.

300
00:19:59,620 --> 00:20:03,155
I mean, I'm only her buddy
because Ms. Ayers assigned her to me.

301
00:20:03,232 --> 00:20:05,226
That does not mean
I am her friend.

302
00:20:07,213 --> 00:20:10,016
I'll make sure her doctors
are all clear on that.

303
00:20:10,089 --> 00:20:12,027
Thanks.

304
00:20:12,096 --> 00:20:15,402
So, has she ever said anything to you
about diet pills?

305
00:20:15,474 --> 00:20:18,176
- Ha. She told you that too?
- What do you mean?

306
00:20:18,251 --> 00:20:20,189
I totally busted her
for taking drugs one day.

307
00:20:20,258 --> 00:20:23,793
She totally lied, said that they were
diet pills her mom had given her.

308
00:20:23,870 --> 00:20:27,314
Come on. Get real.
No way a girl like that
is taking diet pills.

309
00:20:28,486 --> 00:20:31,359
I didn't give her diet pills.
I would never do that.

310
00:20:31,428 --> 00:20:33,366
Right. So it was
her imaginary mom.

311
00:20:33,435 --> 00:20:35,406
She didn't take any pills.
The girl's lying.

312
00:20:35,476 --> 00:20:38,577
Why would she lie?
Because she's another mean littlejerk.

313
00:20:38,653 --> 00:20:42,324
- Mom.
- I'm sorry, honey.

314
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:44,999
Clemmie didn't lie.

315
00:20:47,050 --> 00:20:50,618
I did. I took the pills.

316
00:20:52,333 --> 00:20:56,072
I told her you gave them to me
because I didn't wanna get in trouble.

317
00:20:56,147 --> 00:21:00,217
[Foreman]
Where did you get them?
I took them from the store.

318
00:21:01,566 --> 00:21:04,096
Why? Why would you do that?

319
00:21:04,174 --> 00:21:06,373
Because I didn't
wanna be ugly anymore.

320
00:21:06,448 --> 00:21:10,415
- Oh, baby. You're not ugly.
- Yes, I am.

321
00:21:10,496 --> 00:21:13,631
I know you don't think so,
but I am. I'm disgusting.

322
00:21:13,707 --> 00:21:16,580
Jessica, please don't say that.

323
00:21:16,649 --> 00:21:20,925
I just- I just wanted to fit in.

324
00:21:20,998 --> 00:21:22,936
You know, have friends?

325
00:21:23,005 --> 00:21:27,075
Or at least have
one person my age be nice to me.

326
00:21:27,152 --> 00:21:30,596
[Sobs]
Oh.

327
00:21:33,273 --> 00:21:35,211
Listen, the, uh-

328
00:21:35,280 --> 00:21:38,951
The pills cause blood clots,
heart attacks and insomnia.

329
00:21:39,025 --> 00:21:42,491
It explains everything.
We'll keep her overnight to make sure,

330
00:21:42,571 --> 00:21:45,044
but, uh, she'll be fine.

331
00:21:45,114 --> 00:21:48,580
Thank you.
[Sobs]

332
00:21:48,659 --> 00:21:51,098
[Cameron]
I can't believe
she was that desperate.

333
00:21:51,168 --> 00:21:54,041
[House]
Yeah, I'm sure that if
everyone I knew hated me,

334
00:21:54,111 --> 00:21:57,178
couldn't bear to look at me,
I wouldn't go so far as to shoplift.

335
00:21:57,255 --> 00:22:00,857
I'm not talking about the shoplifting.
I'm sure she didn't even know
they were dangerous.

336
00:22:00,934 --> 00:22:04,378
She probably saw them advertised
on TV or over the Internet.

337
00:22:04,446 --> 00:22:08,357
Right. So I guess it's the media
and pharmaceutical companies' fault now,

338
00:22:08,427 --> 00:22:10,992
not the fact that she can't stop shoveling
food down her throat.

339
00:22:11,069 --> 00:22:13,007
No one forced her to get fat.

340
00:22:13,076 --> 00:22:16,484
- No one forced a cancer patient
to get cancer.
- Give me a break. It's not a disease.

341
00:22:16,554 --> 00:22:19,119
Have you seen the latest research?
Yes, I have.

342
00:22:19,197 --> 00:22:23,141
What I haven't seen lately
is a kid eating an apple or riding a bike.

343
00:22:23,210 --> 00:22:26,618
You Americans can't even compete with
the rest of the world in basketball anymore,

344
00:22:26,689 --> 00:22:31,399
unless, of course, it's the type you play
with a remote control on a big-screen TV.

345
00:22:31,471 --> 00:22:34,538
- Right.
- Wait, wait, wait.

346
00:22:34,616 --> 00:22:39,257
Are you gonna let him say that?
He insulted our basketball teams.

347
00:22:39,331 --> 00:22:43,436
[Pager Beeping]

348
00:22:43,512 --> 00:22:46,784
[Pager #2 Beeping]

349
00:22:46,858 --> 00:22:49,526
[Pager #3 Beeping]

350
00:22:49,600 --> 00:22:52,701
[Jessica]
Oh, my God.

351
00:22:54,015 --> 00:22:55,953
It hurts so bad. Please.
What happened?

352
00:22:56,022 --> 00:22:58,426
- She's bleeding.
- From where?

353
00:22:58,497 --> 00:23:01,062
[Sobbing]
Oh, my gosh.

354
00:23:01,140 --> 00:23:05,783
Just please stop it.
Please!

355
00:23:18,533 --> 00:23:21,995
Diet pills brought her to us.
We gave her the sores.

356
00:23:22,074 --> 00:23:24,637
You think she got a staph infection
from something here?

357
00:23:24,713 --> 00:23:27,743
I'm not saying the hospital
gave her the sores.
I'm saying we did, by treating her.

358
00:23:27,822 --> 00:23:30,920
Warfarin-induced skin necrosis.

359
00:23:30,995 --> 00:23:34,663
- Highly unlikely. We started her
on heparin before the warfarin.
- Who gave her the heparin?

360
00:23:34,738 --> 00:23:38,109
- I did warfarin. She did heparin.
- Sure you didn't both give her warfarin?

361
00:23:38,180 --> 00:23:40,173
Yes. I did not screw up.

362
00:23:42,224 --> 00:23:46,097
Did you actually see her prepare
and administer the heparin?

363
00:23:48,707 --> 00:23:52,443
- [Sighs]
- 'Nuff said.

364
00:23:52,516 --> 00:23:55,648
You were standing right there.
I was preparing my own dose.

365
00:23:55,724 --> 00:24:00,394
- Yeah, right.
There's gotta be some other cause.
- None that I can think of.

366
00:24:00,470 --> 00:24:02,964
Let's fix the mistake.

367
00:24:03,042 --> 00:24:07,211
Give her unfractionated I. V. Heparin
and low molecular weight heparin
by subcutaneous injection, stat.

368
00:24:13,202 --> 00:24:15,263
Making me look bad
is not gonna save your job.

369
00:24:15,339 --> 00:24:17,468
You think you're incapable
of making a mistake?

370
00:24:17,545 --> 00:24:19,708
You think that I'm just
gonna roll over and take this?

371
00:24:19,785 --> 00:24:22,222
House isn't gonna protect you
just because you kiss his ass.

372
00:24:22,290 --> 00:24:25,057
Vogler wants to know
what he can do for me.

373
00:24:25,130 --> 00:24:30,096
Hey! Stop worrying about your asses
and start worrying about the patient's.

374
00:24:49,825 --> 00:24:51,818
She sleeping?

375
00:24:51,897 --> 00:24:55,200
As a result of the sedatives, yeah.
Can't let her wake up. Too much pain.

376
00:24:58,480 --> 00:25:03,618
"Warfarin-induced skin necrosis."

377
00:25:03,694 --> 00:25:06,531
I... have no idea what that means.

378
00:25:06,600 --> 00:25:10,803
But it says here
we gave her the warfarin.

379
00:25:10,877 --> 00:25:14,750
And I do know what "induced" means.
We did this?

380
00:25:14,822 --> 00:25:18,592
At this point,
it's not exactly clear.

381
00:25:20,334 --> 00:25:22,531
You should probably talk
to Dr. House.

382
00:25:22,607 --> 00:25:25,842
Oh. You two need time
to get your stories straight.

383
00:25:25,915 --> 00:25:27,908
He doesn't tell me what to do.

384
00:25:27,987 --> 00:25:31,757
So you don't just blindly follow
his commands. You're your own man.

385
00:25:31,830 --> 00:25:35,794
And yet here you are,
working for a guy you can't stand.

386
00:25:35,874 --> 00:25:38,437
I respect him.
What exactly is it you respect?

387
00:25:38,513 --> 00:25:42,477
His attitude toward humanity?
He thinks we're all idiots and liars.

388
00:25:42,556 --> 00:25:46,326
How about his attitude toward you?
Plays with you like a cat
with a ball of string.

389
00:25:46,399 --> 00:25:50,397
What do you want?
I wanna know
if you wanna keep your job.

390
00:25:50,477 --> 00:25:52,572
If he chooses to let me go,
I can live with that.

391
00:25:52,649 --> 00:25:55,120
- That's not an answer.
- Are you offering to protect me?

392
00:25:55,188 --> 00:25:57,659
- Still not an answer.
- I want my job.

393
00:26:03,476 --> 00:26:05,709
Dr. Chase.
Boss.

394
00:26:10,158 --> 00:26:15,101
What was that about?
He wanted to know
what warfarin is. I don't know.

395
00:26:40,067 --> 00:26:42,663
Brr. Icy.

396
00:26:44,711 --> 00:26:48,379
I'll definitely think twice before
correcting one of your mistakes again.

397
00:26:48,454 --> 00:26:52,122
Correct all you want.
Course, it's a bit more productive
if there's an actual mistake.

398
00:26:52,196 --> 00:26:55,795
Right. I always forget that part.

399
00:26:55,872 --> 00:26:59,836
I gave her the heparin,
which means the necrosis
is not a reaction to the warfarin,

400
00:26:59,916 --> 00:27:04,655
which is probably why
she's not responding to your treatment.
Yet.

401
00:27:07,702 --> 00:27:10,469
If you didn't screw up,
then what is it?

402
00:27:12,614 --> 00:27:15,381
You don't have an answer.
Yet.

403
00:27:15,455 --> 00:27:18,120
When you come up with something,
let me know.

404
00:27:18,194 --> 00:27:21,964
I'll be in the clinic, warming up.

405
00:27:22,038 --> 00:27:25,500
I'm the only one
who's always stood behind you
when you've screwed up.

406
00:27:25,580 --> 00:27:27,709
Why? Why would you
support someone who screws up?

407
00:27:27,786 --> 00:27:31,784
Because I'm not insanely insecure,
and because I can actually trust
in another human being,

408
00:27:31,862 --> 00:27:34,800
and I am not an angry,
misanthropic son of a bitch.

409
00:27:34,869 --> 00:27:38,104
I'm sorry.
You said you weren't angry.

410
00:27:40,116 --> 00:27:43,248
Who would you fire?

411
00:27:43,324 --> 00:27:45,852
[Sighs]
No one.

412
00:27:45,931 --> 00:27:47,901
Not an option.

413
00:27:47,969 --> 00:27:52,469
If everyone took a pay cut and put in
a few more hours, we could all stay
for the same amount of money.

414
00:27:52,547 --> 00:27:55,714
Figures you'd try and come up with
a solution where no one gets hurt.

415
00:27:55,789 --> 00:27:59,058
The problem is, the world doesn't work
that way just 'cause you want it to.

416
00:27:59,130 --> 00:28:02,102
Figures you'd stall
and refuse to deal with the issue.

417
00:28:02,170 --> 00:28:05,666
Problem is, the world doesn't go away
just because you want it to.

418
00:28:05,746 --> 00:28:08,445
[Sighs]

419
00:28:22,956 --> 00:28:24,983
Excuse me. Dr. House?

420
00:28:25,061 --> 00:28:28,159
My wife saw you yesterday.
Lucille Hernandez?

421
00:28:28,236 --> 00:28:30,206
Uh, he's not in today.

422
00:28:30,274 --> 00:28:32,905
My wife said
he walked with a cane.

423
00:28:32,980 --> 00:28:37,252
He's also got a bit of a drug problem.
Sometimes doesn't show up for weeks.

424
00:28:39,330 --> 00:28:41,926
[Cuddy]
The M.R.I. 's are rented, but, um-

425
00:28:43,406 --> 00:28:46,243
Did you make a decision?
He's not gonna fire anybody.

426
00:28:46,314 --> 00:28:50,415
Yes. I'm gonna cut the pay
of all four of us.

427
00:28:50,491 --> 00:28:55,025
Seventeen percent across the board
will allow you to keep us all
for the same amount of money.

428
00:28:55,103 --> 00:28:57,096
I believe it's what
you suits call a "win-win".

429
00:28:58,778 --> 00:29:01,545
All right, uh, i-if you can-
No.

430
00:29:01,618 --> 00:29:04,818
Lfhe can work it so we keep the current
staff for the same amount of money,

431
00:29:04,894 --> 00:29:07,490
what difference does it make?

432
00:29:10,407 --> 00:29:13,174
It's not about the money.

433
00:29:13,248 --> 00:29:16,380
This is not a negotiation.
It never was.

434
00:29:16,455 --> 00:29:19,018
I need to know that
whatever I ask you to do,

435
00:29:19,095 --> 00:29:22,090
however distasteful
you find it, you'll do it.

436
00:29:22,170 --> 00:29:25,200
And just as importantly,
you need to know that.

437
00:29:27,083 --> 00:29:28,881
[Sighs]

438
00:29:32,628 --> 00:29:34,621
[Door Closes]

439
00:29:35,904 --> 00:29:37,897
What's going on with my wife?

440
00:29:37,976 --> 00:29:41,313
[Sighs]
Even if I was Dr. House,

441
00:29:41,385 --> 00:29:45,292
physician-patient confidentiality
protects me from annoying conversations.

442
00:29:45,361 --> 00:29:49,462
She told me about the tumor.
Yeah? She also tell you
why she's refusing to have it removed?

443
00:29:49,538 --> 00:29:53,502
I don't care about a scar.
And she can always gain the weight back.

444
00:29:53,581 --> 00:29:59,550
- You want her to regain the weight?
- Yeah. I mean, only if she wants to.

445
00:29:59,630 --> 00:30:03,902
Why?
I've always thought she looked sexiest
when she was pregnant.

446
00:30:03,973 --> 00:30:08,211
Something about knowing
she's a mother just makes me want to-
Tell her that and leave me alone.

447
00:30:08,284 --> 00:30:12,818
I did. You gotta talk to her. I couldn't
bear it if something happened to her.

448
00:30:12,895 --> 00:30:16,734
The tumor is benign.
Nothing's gonna happen,
except maybe some more heartburn.

449
00:30:18,175 --> 00:30:20,338
What if it gets even bigger,
or it changes?

450
00:30:20,415 --> 00:30:23,582
You know where to find us.
Building's not going anywhere.

451
00:30:23,656 --> 00:30:29,330
Tell her it's cancer. You obviously
don't have a problem with lying.
Oh. Way to win me over.

452
00:30:29,403 --> 00:30:32,899
We got six kids.
She can't afford to take a chance.

453
00:30:32,980 --> 00:30:35,611
You have kids. How novel.
That changes everything.

454
00:30:35,685 --> 00:30:38,281
So if Mommy gets heartburn,
one of them might catch on fire.

455
00:30:38,360 --> 00:30:42,803
Please. I don't know what we'd do.

456
00:30:48,919 --> 00:30:51,720
They are cute.

457
00:30:51,792 --> 00:30:53,887
Have her come back in.
What?

458
00:30:53,965 --> 00:30:57,097
Your plight has moved me.
Tell your wife to come back.
[Elevator Bell Dings]

459
00:31:03,923 --> 00:31:05,893
The necrosis is getting worse.

460
00:31:05,962 --> 00:31:08,433
Maybe because we're treating her
for the wrong thing.

461
00:31:08,500 --> 00:31:12,270
- Have you found the right thing?
- No.

462
00:31:12,344 --> 00:31:16,080
Then we continue the treatment,
hope it's just taking longer
than it should.

463
00:31:16,153 --> 00:31:19,125
At this point, it doesn't matter
what caused the necrosis.

464
00:31:19,194 --> 00:31:23,260
- Or who.
- [Wilson] If we don't stop it from spreading,
it'll kill her before the end of the day.

465
00:31:23,338 --> 00:31:27,781
What else can we do?
Get rid of it. Remove the dying flesh
before it penetrates the abdominal wall.

466
00:31:29,687 --> 00:31:31,680
Do it.

467
00:31:32,795 --> 00:31:36,064
There's still a chance the heparin
treatment could start to take effect.

468
00:31:36,136 --> 00:31:39,598
We're gonna wait as long as we can,
but if there's no change
in the next few hours,

469
00:31:39,679 --> 00:31:41,946
we're gonna have to treat
the symptoms directly.

470
00:31:42,018 --> 00:31:45,321
So you can get rid of the sores?
Through surgery.

471
00:31:45,392 --> 00:31:48,490
Technically, it's an amputation.

472
00:31:48,567 --> 00:31:51,665
Amputation? But the sores are-

473
00:31:51,742 --> 00:31:56,549
Warfarin-induced necrosis
attacks fatty tissue,
mainly in the breasts.

474
00:31:56,620 --> 00:32:02,259
Wait. Are you talking about cutting off
my daughter's... breasts?

475
00:32:07,080 --> 00:32:11,386
- She's 10 years old.
- A radical mastectomy
may be her only chance for survival.

476
00:32:13,530 --> 00:32:17,200
I'm sorry, but I'm gonna
have to ask you to sign this.

477
00:32:28,500 --> 00:32:31,898
[Keyboard Clacking]

478
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:35,089
[Door Opens]
Could we talk?

479
00:32:38,098 --> 00:32:40,654
What, no roses, no chocolates?

480
00:32:40,730 --> 00:32:43,660
If you're here to apologize-
I'm not here to apologize.

481
00:32:43,730 --> 00:32:46,456
Uh-oh.

482
00:32:47,729 --> 00:32:50,318
That means you're here
for something more complicated.

483
00:32:50,394 --> 00:32:53,223
Do you want to fire me?

484
00:32:54,994 --> 00:32:59,720
Yes. Just waiting for an excuse.
Thank God Vogler came along. Whew.

485
00:32:59,793 --> 00:33:03,553
It's the only reason I can think of why
you're insisting that I made a mistake.

486
00:33:03,625 --> 00:33:07,078
Really? Because there is
another explanation.

487
00:33:07,158 --> 00:33:09,385
Perhaps not as much fun
as your Freudian analysis,

488
00:33:09,457 --> 00:33:11,444
but maybe you actually
made a mistake.

489
00:33:11,523 --> 00:33:14,612
You're doing this because
you can't deal with your feelings for me.

490
00:33:19,789 --> 00:33:24,310
I believe that you are
the only one to express feelings.

491
00:33:24,387 --> 00:33:28,942
And if we're gonna look at this
from a first-year psych point of view,
maybe you want me to fire you.

492
00:33:29,019 --> 00:33:31,778
Maybe that's why
you're acting weird-
You're the one being different.

493
00:33:31,852 --> 00:33:34,839
You're always pushing things,
pushing the rules, pushing us.
But not this time.

494
00:33:34,918 --> 00:33:38,110
You jumped on this idea
like a life raft. Not one question
about what else it could be.

495
00:33:38,184 --> 00:33:42,137
No riding us for other answers.
I have the answer.

496
00:33:43,816 --> 00:33:47,803
Then why aren't you watching TV
or playing your damn Game Boy...

497
00:33:47,882 --> 00:33:50,711
or whatever else you have
so much fun doing by yourself?

498
00:33:53,548 --> 00:33:56,206
Maybe I should just quit.

499
00:33:57,346 --> 00:34:00,402
Make it easy for everyone.

500
00:34:00,479 --> 00:34:02,466
Maybe you should.

501
00:34:02,545 --> 00:34:05,066
[Sighs]

502
00:34:08,611 --> 00:34:10,598
[House]
Men are pigs.

503
00:34:10,677 --> 00:34:12,733
You called me in to tell me-

504
00:34:12,809 --> 00:34:17,762
I should've realized the vasectomy
and condoms was overkill,
but this was too obvious to miss.

505
00:34:19,275 --> 00:34:21,967
Cute kids.

506
00:34:22,041 --> 00:34:26,233
Love her green eyes
and his baby blues.

507
00:34:26,307 --> 00:34:30,237
- Of course, since both you
and your husband have brown eyes-
- Where'd you get that?

508
00:34:30,305 --> 00:34:35,361
From the father of three, maximum four,
of your six children.

509
00:34:35,438 --> 00:34:37,766
So I'm thinking maybe
the reason you don't want surgery...

510
00:34:37,837 --> 00:34:40,700
is that while your husband will
find you attractive no matter what,

511
00:34:40,771 --> 00:34:44,895
all the other men you're sleeping with
might not be so open-minded.

512
00:34:44,969 --> 00:34:48,627
Which brings me back
to my original thesis: Men are pigs.

513
00:34:48,702 --> 00:34:54,098
You got nothing to worry about.
They'll pretty much
have sex with anyone:

514
00:34:54,167 --> 00:34:59,621
Fat, skinny, married, single,
complete strangers, relatives-

515
00:34:59,700 --> 00:35:03,289
You... are sick.
So are you.

516
00:35:03,365 --> 00:35:06,057
And I'm sure there are Web sites
full of men...

517
00:35:06,132 --> 00:35:09,029
Iooking for married women
with surgical scars.

518
00:35:10,563 --> 00:35:14,585
So have the surgery. Please?

519
00:35:14,662 --> 00:35:17,354
Okay.

520
00:35:19,461 --> 00:35:21,618
[Door Closes]

521
00:35:23,494 --> 00:35:25,481
Thanks.

522
00:35:28,459 --> 00:35:31,288
Why have you
been talking to Cameron?

523
00:35:31,358 --> 00:35:35,550
- If House picks you,
I'll be needing a new source in that room.
- If he picks me?

524
00:35:35,625 --> 00:35:40,681
Sure. Foreman's smarter.
House has got a thing for Cameron.

525
00:35:40,757 --> 00:35:43,449
I've been feeding you information
so you'll protect me.

526
00:35:43,523 --> 00:35:45,613
And I will protect you
as long as I need you.

527
00:35:45,690 --> 00:35:47,950
And you will feed me information
as long as you need me.

528
00:35:48,022 --> 00:35:50,885
I spoke with Cameron
because if I have alternatives,

529
00:35:50,955 --> 00:35:53,885
I don't need you.

530
00:35:57,286 --> 00:35:59,580
She's not gonna rat on House.

531
00:35:59,652 --> 00:36:02,445
Foreman never said anything
about talkin' to me?

532
00:36:05,418 --> 00:36:08,110
Interesting, huh?

533
00:36:09,617 --> 00:36:11,377
[Door Closes]

534
00:36:26,546 --> 00:36:31,602
It's been almost three hours.
Still no change in her condition.

535
00:36:31,679 --> 00:36:34,666
I think we should
get her into surgery.

536
00:36:34,745 --> 00:36:36,801
So what do you wanna do?

537
00:36:39,076 --> 00:36:42,404
Assume that Cameron
didn't screw up.

538
00:36:44,210 --> 00:36:47,970
What if it's not the warfarin?
It has to be. The sores presented
right after we administered it.

539
00:36:48,042 --> 00:36:52,268
Right, right, right. But let's just say it's not.
Come on. Come on. What do you got?

540
00:36:52,340 --> 00:36:56,998
Can I have a second to think?
No. There's no time to think. Just say
the first thing that comes into your head.

541
00:36:57,073 --> 00:36:59,765
She's fat.
Enough already, okay?
We got it. You hate fat people.

542
00:36:59,840 --> 00:37:03,066
That's not what I meant.
We already considered obesity
as a cause.

543
00:37:03,138 --> 00:37:07,001
So did all her other doctors.
No, I mean what if it's not a cause?
What if it's a symptom?

544
00:37:08,404 --> 00:37:13,357
Okay. So, what could cause obesity
and skin necrosis?

545
00:37:15,303 --> 00:37:17,767
I don't care if it makes sense.
Just give me something.

546
00:37:17,835 --> 00:37:22,163
- Ulcers secondary to vasculitis.
- No, that's just sores, not obesity.

547
00:37:22,234 --> 00:37:24,755
- Pyoderma gangrenosum.
- More sores.

548
00:37:24,834 --> 00:37:28,764
Let's look at it from the other side.
What has obesity as a symptom?

549
00:37:28,833 --> 00:37:32,264
Hypothyroidism?
Genetics are more likely.
Her mom's heavy too.

550
00:37:37,164 --> 00:37:40,719
She's not just heavy, she's tall.

551
00:37:41,997 --> 00:37:44,154
We have any history
on the dad?
Yeah.

552
00:37:46,229 --> 00:37:48,251
6'1 ".

553
00:37:51,661 --> 00:37:54,125
Kid's short.

554
00:37:54,194 --> 00:37:58,749
We got stunted growth,
high blood pressure, blood clots, obesity-

555
00:38:00,326 --> 00:38:02,984
- It's Cushing's.
- No. Necrosis doesn't present-

556
00:38:03,058 --> 00:38:05,887
In rare cases,
Cushing's can cause hypercalcemia,

557
00:38:05,958 --> 00:38:08,751
which can lead
to the same skin necrosis as warfarin.

558
00:38:08,824 --> 00:38:11,186
It's perfect.
It explains everything.

559
00:38:11,256 --> 00:38:16,152
Except it's not Cushing's.
She's had multiple blood tests,
and none show abnormal cortisol levels.

560
00:38:16,222 --> 00:38:19,516
The hypercortisolism could be cyclical.
We didn't catch it in the right phase.

561
00:38:19,588 --> 00:38:23,678
- We'll have to do another U.F.C. -
- There's no time. We've got
less than an hour to make a call.

562
00:38:23,753 --> 00:38:26,081
If we treat for Cushing's
and we're wrong, she's dead.

563
00:38:26,153 --> 00:38:29,548
If we assume it's not Cushing's,
she'll lose her breast and may still be sick.

564
00:38:32,885 --> 00:38:37,009
- Do an M.R.I.
- You want us to look
for hypercortisolism with an M.R.I.?

565
00:38:37,085 --> 00:38:41,311
No, I want you to look for what could
cause hypercortisolism with an M.R.I.

566
00:38:48,481 --> 00:38:51,344
[Motor Whirring]

567
00:39:00,813 --> 00:39:03,471
[Foreman]
Nothing on the adrenals.

568
00:39:05,778 --> 00:39:08,367
Heard Cameron went home.
Is she sick?

569
00:39:08,444 --> 00:39:10,965
Go back to the pituitary views.

570
00:39:11,043 --> 00:39:14,166
- She seemed okay.
- Think she's got
another reason for leaving?

571
00:39:14,242 --> 00:39:16,536
I hope so. Wait, stop.

572
00:39:16,608 --> 00:39:19,038
There. What's that?

573
00:39:22,541 --> 00:39:25,994
Huh. A tumor.

574
00:39:26,074 --> 00:39:28,061
It's Cushing's.

575
00:39:28,139 --> 00:39:33,126
The tumor causes Cushing's.
Cushing's messes with hormone production.

576
00:39:33,205 --> 00:39:35,533
Hormones control everything:
Growth, weight-

577
00:39:35,604 --> 00:39:39,557
Can you fix it?
She'll need surgery
to remove the tumor.

578
00:39:39,637 --> 00:39:42,897
Once it's gone,
everything will get normal very fast.

579
00:39:42,970 --> 00:39:45,366
- No mastectomy?
- No.

580
00:39:45,436 --> 00:39:48,229
Thank God.
The surgery is dangerous.

581
00:39:48,301 --> 00:39:50,595
The pituitary's located
between the cavernous sinuses,

582
00:39:50,668 --> 00:39:52,655
basically right between the eyes.

583
00:39:52,734 --> 00:39:56,221
The area contains the nerves
that control eye movement and
the major arteries that feed the brain.

584
00:39:56,300 --> 00:39:58,162
Oh, my God.

585
00:39:58,233 --> 00:40:01,857
The surgeon will approach
the gland transsphenoidally.

586
00:40:01,932 --> 00:40:04,556
An incision will be made
under the lip,

587
00:40:04,631 --> 00:40:07,789
through which he'll insert
a fiber-optic microscope.

588
00:40:07,864 --> 00:40:12,352
Once the tumor's found, he'll cut it
into small pieces and remove it
through the same hole under the lip.

589
00:40:12,430 --> 00:40:16,861
The whole procedure should take
about three hours, and your daughter
should be able to go home in a few days.

590
00:40:16,929 --> 00:40:20,121
The sores will go away, as well as
her fatigue and the muscle pain.

591
00:40:20,194 --> 00:40:23,181
She'll even start losing weight.

592
00:40:32,025 --> 00:40:35,955
[No Audible Dialogue]

593
00:41:12,550 --> 00:41:14,537
[Foreman]
Jessica.
Hi.

594
00:41:14,616 --> 00:41:18,308
- Is that really you?
- Yep, it's me.

595
00:41:18,382 --> 00:41:21,211
You look fantastic.

596
00:41:21,281 --> 00:41:25,371
- She always looked fantastic.
- Yeah.

597
00:41:53,341 --> 00:41:56,328
- It's been a week.
- Actually, it's over a week.

598
00:41:56,407 --> 00:41:58,394
How have you guys been?

599
00:41:58,472 --> 00:42:00,459
Who is it?

600
00:42:04,605 --> 00:42:06,592
Chase.

601
00:42:08,038 --> 00:42:12,492
No, Chase stays.
Pick someone else.

602
00:42:12,569 --> 00:42:15,692
The deal was-
The deal's changed.

603
00:42:15,769 --> 00:42:19,961
- Pick someone else.
- No.

604
00:42:25,600 --> 00:42:27,587
Mmm.

605
00:42:30,500 --> 00:42:33,021
Pick someone else,
or it'll be the whole department.

606
00:42:36,864 --> 00:42:38,886
[Door Opens]

607
00:44:04,678 --> 00:44:05,938
That's some bad hat, Harry.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
